<title>JAPAN: THAI FIN MIN SAYS WILL KEEP INFLATION DOWN.</title>
<headline>THAI FIN MIN SAYS WILL KEEP INFLATION DOWN.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand Finance Minister Thanong Bidaya said on Monday that his nation will strive to keep inflation under 10 percent and will allow the foreign exchange market to operate without official intervention.</p>
<p>At the same news conference, Japanese officials said that the package would be more than enough for Thailand and that Japan does not see the need for any more financial support.</p>
</text>
